ault Backhand saved by Alex Nedeljkovic","type":{"id":"506","text":"Shot","abbreviation":"shot-on-goal"},"clock":{"displayValue":"2:00"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"10"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"2562602","displayName":"Phillip Danault","shortName":"P. Danault"},"type":"shooter"},{"athlete":{"id":"3114994","displayName":"Alex Nedeljkovic","shortName":"A. Nedeljkovic"},"type":"saver"}]}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"1831","fullName":"Bell Centre","address":{"city":"Montreal","country":"Canada"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/nhl/day/1831.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":20962,"officials":[{"fullName":"Wes McCauley","displayName":"Wes McCauley","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Jesse Marquis","displayName":"Jesse Marquis","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Brandon Blandina","displayName":"Brandon Blandina","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Anthony Lapointe","displayName":"Anthony Lapointe","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Celebrini scores his 2nd goal of the game on an OT power play to lift the Sharks past the Canadiens","description":"— Macklin Celebrini scored his second goal of the game on a power play at 2:13 of overtime to give the San Jose Sharks a 4-3 victory over the Montreal Canadiens on Tuesday night.","story":"MONTREAL -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5206628/macklin-celebrini\">Macklin Celebrini</a> scored his second goal of the game on a power play at 2:13 of overtime to give the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/sj/san-jose-sharks\">San Jose Sharks</a> a 4-3 victory over the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/mtl/montreal-canadiens\">Montreal Canadiens</a> on Tuesday night.\n\n\r\n              Celebrini fired a one-timer into the top-left corner after goalie <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697686/jakub-dobes\">Jakub Dobes</a> was called for interference on Colin Graf.\n\n\r\n              Celebrini added an assist and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5550/tyler-toffoli\">Tyler Toffoli</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5291934/michael-misa\">Michael Misa</a> also scored to help San Jose (5-4-1) rebound from a 3-1 loss to Toronto on Monday night.\n\n\r\n              Sharks goalie <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3114994/alex-nedeljkovic\">Alex Nedeljkovic</a> stopped 31 shots.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4915349/juraj-slafkovsky\">Juraj Slafkovsky</a>, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4565236/cole-caufield\">Cole Caufield</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4233594/nick-suzuki\">Nick Suzuki</a> had a goal and an assist each as Montreal (4-3-2) surrendered a two-goal advantage for the fourth time this season. Dobes made 26 saves.\n\n\r\n              Misa, who hit the post earlier in the period, cut into the Canadiens’ lead at 5:36 in the third, finishing a feed from <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4391255/kiefer-sherwood\">Kiefer Sherwood</a> after Montreal defenseman <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5080230/lane-hutson\">Lane Hutson</a> turned the puck over.\n\n\r\n              Toffoli tied it with 8:51 remaining in regulation when he buried Celebrini’s pass on the power play with <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4893969/arber-xhekaj\">Arber Xhekaj</a> in the penalty box for unsportsmanlike conduct.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Sharks: At Ottawa on Thursday night.\n\n\r\n              Canadiens: At Chicago on Friday night.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-10-21T02:18:09Z"}}